From a93ac605daef46eeb1c4c0cb7f8a8b93b43c7b12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:37:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GLES] GL_GPU_DISJOINT_EXT read once a frame and told
 to every reader of GPU times

GL_GPU_DISJOINT_EXT says that the GPU lost the time since it was last
read (a change of its clocks, a reset), so that the results of the
timer queries in flight are not to be trusted, and reading it clears
it. Five parts of the render thread time their pictures: Kodi's
renderer (the step-down of its chroma), HDR10 adapted to the display,
the passes of the conversion bridge, Dolby Vision rebuilt as HDR10 or
SDR, and native Dolby Vision with its passes. Each read the state
itself, so the first of them in a frame took a notice that the others
never saw, and took the times of a lost period as true.

CGpuDisjoint (GpuDisjoint.h) reads the state in one place of the window
system, once a frame (the first reader after PresentRender() reads
it), and counts the disjoint periods; each reader keeps the count it
last saw and learns of every period since, whatever frame it asks in
and in whatever order. A reader that has just made its timers takes no
period of before. Kodi's renderer asks the window system, and reads the
state itself only where the window system is not GBM's.
